                        <annot xml:id="ue1937-III-annot-m018-grace-slur" type="editorial" label="encoding-note" plist="#ue1937-III-slur-L144F1-L145F1N1 #ue1937-III-note-L144F1 #ue1937-III-note-L145F1S2" facs="#zone-ue1937-III-m018" resp="#resp.editor" source="#src.ue1937">
                           <p>UE p. 8 prints the short G-sharp4 grace-note slur below, ending on the upper B-flat4 (L145F1S2), not the lower B-natural3 or the whole chord. Verovio 6.3.0-425dd7b draws a lower curve beneath the whole chord even when endid identifies the upper note. As in bar 15, the editor-approved workaround is curvedir="above", retaining the note-specific endpoint for analysis and recording the printed lower direction here. The separate cross-staff slur from bar 17 is unchanged. See <ref target="https://github.com/rism-digital/verovio/issues/4313">Verovio issue 4313</ref>.</p>
                        </annot>
