                        <annot xml:id="ue1937-III-annot-m042-grace-slur" type="editorial" label="encoding-note" plist="#ue1937-III-slur-L360F2-L361F2 #ue1937-III-note-L360F2 #ue1937-III-note-L361F2" facs="#zone-ue1937-III-m042" resp="#resp.editor" source="#src.ue1937">
                           <p>UE p. 9 prints an upper slur from the B-flat5 grace note (L360F2) to the single D-natural5 (L361F2). The source direction and note-specific endpoint are retained. Unlike bars 15 and 18, the target is not a chord member, so this case does not exhibit their chord-attachment ambiguity in Verovio 6.3.0-425dd7b. The curve uses the default layout without manual offsets; no rendering workaround is applied.</p>
                        </annot>
