                        <beamSpan xml:id="ue1937-III-beamSpan-L478F2-L482F2" staff="1" startid="#ue1937-III-note-L478F2" endid="#ue1937-III-note-L482F2" plist="#ue1937-III-note-L478F2 #ue1937-III-rest-L481F2 #ue1937-III-note-L482F2" />
                        <annot xml:id="ue1937-III-annot-m051-052-beam-height" type="editorial" label="encoding-note" plist="#ue1937-III-beamSpan-L478F2-L482F2 #ue1937-III-rest-L481F2" facs="#zone-ue1937-III-m051 #zone-ue1937-III-m052" resp="#resp.editor" source="#src.ue1937">
                           <p>The RH beam from L478F2 to L482F2 continues across the system break over the initial eighth rest L481F2 in bar 52. Verovio 6.3.0-425dd7b draws the continuation through that rest; the editor requests a slightly lower beam. Increasing stem.len on either or both endpoint notes, specifying beamSpan/@place="below", or changing @slope does not lower it. MEI 5.1 CMN does not permit @vo on beamSpan. The source beam grouping, note-specific endpoints and rest position are retained without ineffective engraving attributes. See <ref target="https://github.com/rism-digital/verovio/issues/932">Verovio issue 932</ref>.</p>
                        </annot>
